      {
        "question": "Can you machine a non-standard flange from my drawing?",
        "answer": "Yes. Share the bore, bolt pattern, pilot register, sealing arrangement and mounting geometry. These features are reviewed together to define the machining datums, finishing allowances and inspection plan.",
        "points": [
          "Include a 2D drawing and 3D model where available.",
          "Identify the dimensions that control fit, sealing or alignment."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I specify for robot and motor mounting flanges?",
        "answer": "Define the mating pilot, bolt circle, mounting face and any shaft or cable clearance. Include the relevant interface standard where applicable and identify customer-specific geometry or positioning requirements."
      },
      {
        "question": "What information is needed for vacuum or sealing flanges?",
        "answer": "State the mating flange type, sealing method, material, surface finish and any cleaning requirements. Include O-ring grooves, knife-edge geometry or other sealing details on the approved drawing."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which materials, finishes and inspection records are available?",
        "answer": "Material options include aluminum, stainless steel, carbon and alloy steel, brass, titanium and nickel alloys. Finishing and documentation are agreed for the specific material and application.",
        "points": [
          "Specify material certificates, dimensional reports and any PPAP or FAIR requirements with the enquiry."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I request a custom flange quote?",
        "answer": "Send your drawing or model, material, quantity, critical tolerances, surface finish and requested delivery date. Include the mating interface and any sealing, cleaning or documentation requirements so the quote covers the full scope."
      }
