    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Which semiconductor housings can you machine?",
        "answer": "The range includes sensor bodies, camera housings, detector tubes, laser-module bodies, optical alignment housings and encoder enclosures. Send the part and assembly drawings so the geometry and machining route can be reviewed."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do these housings need turning, milling or both?",
        "answer": "Round bodies, stepped bores and threaded diameters may suit turning. Mounting flats, pockets, cross-holes and connector openings can require milling. The drawing, material, workholding and critical feature relationships determine the process."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I include with a quote request?",
        "answer": "Provide a 2D drawing and 3D model, material and condition, quantities, finish and requested delivery date. Identify sensor and lens seats, alignment datums, seal faces, thread specifications and the inspection records required."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I specify vacuum or cleanroom requirements?",
        "answer": "Yes. Include the intended environment, surface requirements, cleaning acceptance criteria and packaging instructions. Any outgassing, leak, particle or other qualification testing must be reviewed and agreed for the specific part and process."
      },
      {
        "question": "How are tolerances and surface finishes confirmed?",
        "answer": "Mark critical bore sizes, datum relationships, mounting faces and surface finish requirements on the drawing. Feasibility and inspection methods are reviewed against the material, geometry, coating allowances and order quantity."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which material and production records can I request?",
        "answer": "Request material certificates, drawing revision records, dimensional reports and finishing records with the enquiry. First-article inspection, additional testing and repeat-batch documentation are confirmed in the agreed order scope."
      }
    ],
