    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is the difference between a bearing bushing and a bearing housing?",
        "answer": "A bearing bushing provides a sliding interface for a shaft or pivot pin. A bearing housing is the supporting body that locates a bushing or a separate bearing. This page covers custom machined sleeves and bushings."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which bushing designs can you machine?",
        "answer": "We review plain sleeves, flanged bushings, stepped profiles, grooves, slots and cross-drilled features against your drawing. The machining route depends on material, wall thickness, feature access and order quantity."
      },
      {
        "question": "What information is needed to quote a custom precision bearing bushing?",
        "answer": "Send the 2D drawing and a 3D model where available, material grade, quantity, surface requirements and delivery needs. Identify bore and outside-diameter fits, mating parts and any inspection or certification requirements.",
        "points": [
          "Include flange dimensions, lubrication features and the current drawing revision.",
          "State whether critical bore checks apply before or after installation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Can you supply bushings with a specified press fit or running clearance?",
        "answer": "We machine to the dimensions and limits agreed on the drawing. Review the shaft and housing dimensions together with material and installation conditions. Do not assume that a free-state bore measurement alone defines the final assembled clearance."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can every bearing bushing operate without lubrication?",
        "answer": "Lubrication requirements depend on the material system, mating shaft, load, speed and operating environment. A solid machined metal bushing should not be assumed to be self-lubricating. Identify any specified liner, lubricant inserts or porous bearing material separately so the supply and manufacturing route can be confirmed."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which inspection records and production quantities can be quoted?",
        "answer": "Prototype and repeat-production enquiries are reviewed individually. Material certificates, dimensional reports and customer-specific first-article records can be included in the quotation scope. Price and delivery follow review of the drawing, quantity, material availability, finishing and inspection requirements."
      }
    ],
